subproblem.statement:
Let N ∈ ℕ, R ∈ ℝ, w, s : ℝ^N → ℝ, and ψ_j : ℝ^N → ℝ for j ∈ ℕ. Assume that:
- w is integrable with respect to Lebesgue measure L^N on the open ball B := B_R(0);
- every ψ_j is L^N-a.e.-strongly measurable;
- |ψ_j(y)| ≤ 1 for all j and all y;
- ψ_j(y) = 0 for all j and all y ∉ B;
- ψ_j(y) → s(y) as j → ∞ for L^N-almost every y.
Then ∫_{ℝ^N} w ψ_j dL^N → ∫_{ℝ^N} w s dL^N as j → ∞.
